🎸
"Lyrics"/en"歌词"/zh-CN"歌詞"/zh-TW
=== start/en
¶The classic Radiohead OK Computer song, Airbag, and it's lyrics, synced to the beat.

A @Scene advances on durations, so its words drift out of step with anything
playing underneath. Here every line carries the /beat/ it is sung on, and
@Beat reports beats as they are heard, so the words and the music can't come
apart. Change @Music/tempo and the whole lyric follows, because nothing here
knows about seconds.

The beats come from a Logic arrangement of the song, so each line lands where
it is actually sung — and that arrangement is what plays underneath, imported
from MIDI as 41 tracks of guitar, bass, strings, drums, bells and horns. The
words and the notes are counting the same beats, so they can only agree.

To set your own words to music, edit @lines and nothing else: each one carries
what to say, the beat it arrives on, how many beats it holds, and which
treatment to use.

Each voice of the arrangement lives in its own source, so no one file is a
wall of notes. Borrowing a source by name gives its last expression — here
a @Track — so the list at the bottom is the whole score.¶
